{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Having Second Thoughts", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Life Is Short", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Third Conditional - Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about situations in the past in a hypothetical context (not real or necessarily true), you can use the structures <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.<br/><br/>   <span class=\"italic\">Could have</span> (+ past participle) means that something was possible in the past, or you had the ability to do something in the past, but that you didn't do it.<br/>Example: <span class=\"italic\">You<span class=\"strong\"> could have lent</span> it to me, but I have a car instead, and that's pretty cool!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should have</span> (+ past participle) means something would have been a good idea, but you didn't do it. You can use it to give advice about the past when you are talking to someone else, or to express regret about what you did or didn't do when you're talking about yourself.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have done</span> so much online shopping.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> ( + past participle) to talk about something you wanted to do but didn't. <br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">would have been kicked out</span> and then he would have been asking to live with me if I hadn't lent it to him.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could/should/would (not) have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hadn't lent it</span> to him, he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have been kicked out</span> and then he would have been asking to live with me.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You shouldn't have done so much online shopping. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " We all have done things we shouldn't have done. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " Like, I shouldn't have given Kevin that loan. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I feel like I should have lent you money when you asked.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You could have lent it to me, but I have a car instead, and that's pretty cool!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bureaucratic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "involving a lot of complicated official rules and processes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must have finished with all the bureaucratic garbage you have had.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about money problems.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "loan", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an amount of money that you borrow from a bank or somebody, an amount of money that you lend somebody", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I shouldn't have given Kevin that loan. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to kick out", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to make someone leave a location, a group, a school, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He would have been kicked out and then he would have been asking to live with me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "student loan  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a loan given to students to pay for their education", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I have bill payments and student loan payments coming up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be strapped for cash", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without money, or low on money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I will be strapped for cash.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to seize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take hold of something suddenly and violently", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Let's not worry about money now, let's just seize the moment!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le11ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Tell your partner about a project at work that took longer or cost more money than you expected.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner what he/she would have done differently?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue reflecting your conversation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read it aloud together.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about money or work.", "type": "text